Publication-contract fixture notice

This directory contains twelve original fictional source/candidate cases under
the repository LICENSE. Widget and WidgetCo are invented for tests; CVE-shaped
identifiers, timestamps and history checksums are sample values, not statements
about real vulnerabilities or publications. All source URLs use reserved .example
names. No captured production draft, CVE record, third-party advisory text, or
live model output is retained.

Three captured incident artifacts imported during integration were removed in
full, rather than asserting redistribution rights over their contents. New
fictional candidates preserve the missing-guidance and corrected-notice cases.
A separate marketplace-product-label case checks canonical product naming.
The parent provenance.json records the imported revision, removed-file hashes,
transformation and hashes of all current inputs. No new license is assigned to
the removed material.

Expected accept/reject labels express the publication requirements. Each case
crosses manual validation, stored-brief public rendering/backfill, durable outbox
with restart, and same-identity replacement. Rejected replacements must preserve
the previous durable snapshot. The repair case also passes an authored response
that omits the body through the real repair path and publication validation.
The baseline requires every case, every route and full acceptance/rejection
recall. Missing required inputs fail; they do not skip the gate.

Run the combined offline extraction and publication contract gate:
  go test ./internal/eval -run '^TestEvalGate$' -count=1

This is deterministic contract validation, not measured model accuracy, factual
grounding accuracy, paid inference, or a production-savings benchmark. Live
experiments through cmd/eval are separate and may incur provider charges.
